    "segments": [
      {
        "id": "seg-01",
        "chapter_id": "ch-01",
        "text": "This is Willow Run, Michigan, seen from space by Landsat satellites, one summer at a time from 1984 to 2026. Between 2001 and 2002, about 4 hectares were cleared or built over in the southeast.",
        "year_from": 1984,
        "year_to": 2012,
        "claim_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-02",
        "chapter_id": "ch-03",
        "text": "Between 2013 and 2014, about 6 hectares that looked like bare or built-up ground changed to something else in the centre. Part of it may come from switching Landsat satellites. One report says: The runway at Willow Run Airport was reconstructed using nearly 50,000 cubic yards of concrete. One report also says: The former Willow Run GM Powertrain plant was slated for demolition beginning in October. The change held for three summers in the record. Compare the 2013 and 2014 frames to see it.",
        "year_from": 2013,
        "year_to": 2014,
        "claim_ids": [
          "cl-01",
          "cl-02"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-03",
        "chapter_id": "ch-07",
        "text": "Between 2017 and 2018, about 5 hectares were cleared or built over in the southeast. Between 2017 and 2018, about 6 hectares turned greener in the centre. Between 2022 and 2023, about 9 hectares turned greener in the centre. That is how Willow Run, Michigan has changed since 1984.",
